  "source_changes": [
    "Start with the current canonical protocol source; add only scratch harness accessors, stage8 single-attempt retry seam, buffer ownership and byte insertion changes.",
    "Use stage8 validated two-Task driver unchanged: successful flush reenters the loop before a read; postyield write makes one immediate attempt before the existing async fallback.",
    "Each raw owner Task allocates two uninitialized 64KiB blocks through its same system AllocatorRef, with explicit null checks and partial-allocation cleanup. Span metadata is zero-initialized, payload is not.",
    "Pending bytes are read only inside [begin,end) after native encoding copied them; input bytes are read only up to a successful recv/await result length. Allocation never substitutes unread uninitialized bytes for received data.",
    "raw_data_chunk retains its capacity/error/compaction rules, but inserts the actual received bytes directly instead of resize-value-initializing bytes and overwriting them.",
    "Reserve original streams capacity on the owner Task before callbacks. On completion/failure delete native session before freeing readable/stream containers and wire blocks; close the socket before Task return and before both external joins finish.",
    "Keep current canonical RawHarness worker_ declared after every field its new thread can read. Its persistent manual thread remains inactive in both measured arms."
  ],
