  "interpretation": [
    "In AB Hyle median elapsed is about 1.42% above raw; in BA Hyle median is about 0.11% below raw. This fixed control does not show a consistent gap of the formal manual-loop comparison's size.",
    "Process drift is retained: Hyle median +1.28735%, raw +2.83595% from AB to BA; all epoch ranges and raw measurements remain. Mean and median need not produce the same tiny BA ordering.",
    "Do not replace or mark solved the distinct formal manual-loop peer residual. Do not attribute this combined execution-model/driver/ownership difference to pure scheduler or fcontext cost, and do not subtract percentages from prior rounds.",
    "Raw retains default native DATA bounce-copy and its fixed-workload vector representation; accepted Hyle retains owned-wire NO_COPY, generic owner/pin/borrow-ACK/cancel/error/flush epoch responsibilities. These remaining duties differ and are not separately timed.",
    "Matching old TCP header overlay deliberately excludes the later four-line bfea93767 optimization from fresh inline code to match cached HTTP2/core. This is not an all-current-HEAD foundation rebuild."
  ],
  "remaining_different_responsibilities": [
    "Raw provider retains default nghttp2 DATA bounce-copy; accepted Hyle uses the owned-wire NO_COPY callback. The refreshed peer does not silently adopt or remove either path.",
    "Hyle preserves recoverable owner/valid/busy/cancel/deadline checks, pins/borrow-ACK reader lifetime, stream-map/header ownership, typed errors and actual-flush epoch accounting; raw uses its fixed-workload state and vectors. This control does not isolate pure scheduler/fcontext cost.",
    "Raw body vectors are explicitly bounded by the original 64KiB capacity and store every actual DATA byte once before the same verify/consume callbacks; Hyle uses its per-stream receive-ring and public consume API. Container representation/allocation counts need not be identical.",
    "Both encode one native frame before transport write; no frame batching difference is assumed. Window updates follow the original per-chunk native consume calls; do not inject matching frames or credit.",
    "Keep existing terminal semantics and final Event/socket closure. Do not append a raw-only caller-side terminal drain/GOAWAY; differing final queued native control bytes are not forced into equality."
  ],
